# --- KB onboarding contract (Gen 48, 2026-10-23) --------------------------
# KB_POLICY says "all KB is gitignored". That left MANDATORY_STOP.md -- the
# entry file every new seat is told to read FIRST -- outside the repository, so
# it did not survive clone. The KB is the machine's memory; memory must survive
# the machine. These seven files are the onboarding contract set and are
# tracked deliberately. Everything else under knowledge/ stays ignored.
#
# Order matters: negations must follow the ignores they override, and git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded. Hence the
# directory negation + re-ignore + re-include shape for personal/ (the same
# shape as the .thoughtmachine/working_docs/ block above).
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/project/MANDATORY_STOP.md
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/project/INFRA_ONBOARDING.md
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/project/working_agreements.md
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/project/security_architecture.md
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/project/status.md
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/project/operator_observations.md
# Gen 54 (2026-10-29) — operator-owned records that must survive a clone:
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/project/hall_of_fame.md
!.thoughtmachine/working_docs/backlog-delivery-arc.md
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/personal/
.thoughtmachine/knowledge/personal/*
!.thoughtmachine/knowledge/personal/handoffs.md

# Gen 50 design pass: auth layer — re-included because docs/* is a catch-all.
!docs/design-auth-layer.md

# --- Source module re-include (Gen 51, 2026-10-26) -----------------------
# `*secret*` above is a deliberate guard against committing secret MATERIAL,
# but it also silently swallowed `agent/config/secret.py` — the redaction
# wrapper module — so a commit of its importers would have shipped a broken
# tree while every test stayed green locally. Re-include the source file only;
# the guard above stays exactly as it is.
!agent/config/secret.py

# Gen 51 logging design pass: sink inventory, redaction truth, deletion
# decidability and the per-call-site keep/delete/unclear marking. Public tier,
# ships with the repo (`docs/*` is a catch-all, so the negation is required).
!docs/design-logging-audit.md

# Gen 51 artifacts published by operator ruling (tier: public, 2026-10-26):
# the agent-core spec and the provider-compatibility findings. Both lived in
# ignored space (docs/* catch-all, .thoughtmachine/working_docs/* re-ignore),
# so `git clean -xdf` would have destroyed them.
!docs/agent-core-spec.md
!docs/provider-compat-findings-2026-10-26.md

# Gen 52 design pass (2026-10-28): the concurrency/affinity design doc and the
# two task briefs written from the running machine. Public tier — the operator
# asked for them saved under docs/. `docs/*` is a catch-all, so each needs its
# own negation line; the directory negation lets git descend into docs/briefs/.
!docs/design-concurrency-and-affinity.md
!docs/briefs/
!docs/briefs/**

# Gen 53 docs/KB catch-up (2026-10-28): the catch-up brief, the post-core-sprint
# integration backlog, and the interruptible-tool-calls design doc. Public tier —
# the operator ruled all three publishable. Two sit in ignored space
# (`.thoughtmachine/working_docs/*` is re-ignored above) and one under the `docs/*`
# catch-all, so each needs its own negation line or `git clean -xdf` would destroy
# them.
!docs/design-interruptible-tool-calls.md
!.thoughtmachine/working_docs/brief-docs-kb-catchup.md
!.thoughtmachine/working_docs/backlog-core-integration.md

